DosSantos_etal_2020-E001,DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1,Br_C,"Table 1, p. 4625, row ""Tragelaphus strepsiceros Br""",21 751 929,21751929,publication_error,21888835128,"Printed whole-brain C (21,751,929) is smaller than the same row's N (4,911,651,549) and I (1,204,929,478), which is impossible, and is 0.1% of Cx + Cb + RoB = 13,064,871,626 + 5,308,593,750 + 3,515,369,752 = 21,888,835,128 (the footnote defines Br as the joint value of Cx, Cb and RoB). Of the 23 species where that sum can be tested, 21 close it within 2%; the other exception is E. myurus (E012). The print dropped the last three digits. Proposed value = the parts sum; it also equals Herculano-Houzel et al. 2015 Table 5 (21,888,835,129), the source Table 1 re-reports. Agrees with the private check against the authors' own data (restricted repo), which is not quoted here.",confirmed,,AI assistant (DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1_internal_check.R) 2026-11-21,2026-11-21,2026-11-21,Printed value read on the PDF page. Substituted in the cell-counts merge (guarded step 3.4e).
DosSantos_etal_2020-E002,DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1,Cb_N,"Table 1, p. 4625, row ""Procavia capensis Cb""",488 3703 000,4883703000,publication_error,488373000,"Printed as ""488 3703 000"", a ten-digit string that reads 4,883,703,000: more neurons than the row's total cells C (579,378,000), impossible. Removing the intruding 0 gives 488,373,000, which (i) equals Br N - Cx N - RoB N = 755,653,256 - 197,933,000 - 69,358,240 = 488,362,016 to 0.002%, (ii) reproduces the printed I/N: 7,806,491 / 488,373,000 = 0.0160 (printed 0.016), and (iii) is the value in Herculano-Houzel et al. 2015 Table 2, the source Table 1 re-reports. Agrees with the private check against the authors' own data (restricted repo), which is not quoted here.",confirmed,,AI assistant (DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1_internal_check.R) 2026-11-21,2026-11-21,2026-11-21,Printed value read on the PDF page. Substituted in the cell-counts merge (guarded step 3.4e).
