DosSantos_etal_2020-E009,DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1,RoB_I,"Table 1, p. 4625, row ""Petrodromus tetradactylus RoB""",1217 665,1217665,publication_ambiguity,1649430,"Two published estimates of the same count disagree. The footnote's formula, I = (I/N) x N = 0.1 x 12,231,811, gives the printed 1,217,665; the measured density gives I/mg x mass = 1845 x 894 = 1,649,430 (-26% for the print). Across the table the two agree within 2% in 129 of 153 rows and within 5% in 144. The density-based values are the coherent set for this species: its printed I/mg values are mass-additive (Cx against Ctx + Hp -0.15%, Br against Cx + Cb + RoB +0.36%), while its printed I column misses the same sums by -2.0% and +2.5%. Table 5 sides with the density: the Afrotheria RoB I/mg range starts at 1845 (this row), and the Afrotheria RoB mean of 100 I/C recomputed from Table 1 is 4.68% with the printed I and 4.89% with the proposed one; Table 5 prints 4.89%. Proposed value = I/mg x mass. Agrees with the private check against the authors' own data (restricted repo), which is not quoted here.",proposed,,AI assistant (DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1_internal_check.R) 2026-11-21,2026-11-21,,Printed value read on the PDF page. Substituted in the cell-counts merge (guarded step 3.4e) pending curator confirmation. The printed I/N of this row then no longer equals I / N; see the I/N erratum for the same row.
