DosSantos_etal_2020-E012,DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1,Br_I,"Table 1, p. 4625, row ""Elephantulus myurus Br*""",2699 666,2699666,publication_ambiguity,,"The species' rows do not close: Br I is -15.6% against Cx + Cb + RoB, Cx I is +12.6% against Ctx + Hp, and Br mass and C miss their sums by -6.0% and -3.5%, although every row is consistent within itself. The table explains it: Cx, Hp and Br carry the footnote mark * (data available for only one specimen of the species), while Cb, RoB and Ctx do not. The starred rows describe one animal and the unstarred rows the species average, so sums across them cannot close. Consistently, Table 5's Afrotheria Cx mean of 100 I/C (6.04%) is reproduced only without this species' single-specimen Cx row (6.04% for the other four species). No cell is misprinted and none is corrected.",confirmed,,AI assistant (DosSantos_etal_2020_Table1_internal_check.R) 2026-11-21,2026-11-21,2026-11-21,Not an error in any one cell; left as printed. Filed under Br I (the largest miss) but applies to all six E. myurus rows: do not combine starred and unstarred rows of this species.
